  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Solve, for the domain $x\\in[0,2\\pi)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin x=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$",
          "worked": "Sine is $-1$ on the negative vertical axis.\n$$x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{7\\pi}{4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt2}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac\\pi4.\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is positive in Q1 and Q4.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac\\pi4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad 2\\pi-\\frac\\pi4\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac{7\\pi}4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$",
          "worked": "Cosine is $1$ on the positive horizontal axis. In $[0,2\\pi)$,\n$$x=0.$$\nThe endpoint $2\\pi$ is excluded.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{6},\\frac{7\\pi}{6}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac1{\\sqrt3}\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac\\pi6.\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is positive in Q1 and Q3.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\frac\\pi6\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\pi+\\frac\\pi6\\\\x&=\\frac\\pi6\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac{7\\pi}6.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos x=-\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{2\\pi}{3},\\frac{4\\pi}{3}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac12\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac\\pi3.\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is negative in Q2 and Q3.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\pi-\\frac\\pi3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\pi+\\frac\\pi3\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pi}3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac{4\\pi}3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\tan x=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{7\\pi}{4}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\tan^{-1}(1)\\\\A&=\\frac\\pi4.\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is negative in Q2 and Q4.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=\\pi-\\frac\\pi4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2\\pi-\\frac\\pi4\\\\x&=\\frac{3\\pi}4\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac{7\\pi}4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
